CHAPTER XVII

INVESTIGATION PROVISIONS

Article 99

( 1) Certain Civil Servant Officials within the Regional Government are granted special authority as investigators to conduct investigations into criminal acts regulated in this Regional Regulation as referred to in the Criminal Procedure Code.

2. The investigative authority as referred to in paragraph (1), is as follows:
a. to receive, search for, collect, and examine information or reports concerning criminal acts relating to the protection of children and women so that such information or reports become more complete and clear;
b. to examine, search for, and collect information regarding individuals or entities about the truth of acts committed in connection with criminal acts relating to the protection of children and women;

c. to request information and evidence from individuals or entities in connection with criminal acts relating to the protection of children and women;
d. to examine books, records, and other documents concerning criminal acts relating to the protection of children and women;

JDIH Kota Singkawang
e. to conduct searches to obtain evidence of bookkeeping, recording, and other documents, as well as to seize such evidence;
f. to request assistance from experts in the framework of carrying out investigative duties for criminal acts relating to the protection of children and women;
g. to order someone to stop and/or prohibit someone from leaving a room or place when an examination is in progress and to examine the identity of persons, objects, and/or documents carried;
h. to photograph persons related to criminal acts relating to the protection of children and women;
i. to summon persons to be heard for their statements and examined as suspects or witnesses;

J. to terminate the investigation; and/or
k. to take other necessary actions for the smooth investigation of criminal acts relating to the protection of children and women in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations.

3. In the event that the investigation meets the elements as referred to in paragraph (1), the Investigator shall notify the commencement of the investigation and submit the results of the investigation to the Public Prosecutor through the Investigator Official of the Police of the Republic of Indonesia, in accordance with the provisions stipulated in the Criminal Procedure Code.
